  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project Output/s</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output/s as listed by the project staff.</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1  Indicator 1</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: 1. Access to energy-efficient green data centers in Thailand increased
2. Best practice green data center design and operations demonstrated in a gender-inclusive manner
3. Local employment generated 
4. Gender equality in the workplace enhanced 
Indicator: 1a. One 25.6 MW Tier III/&#x201c;Rated 3&#x201d;  green data center constructed and obtaining LEED Gold certification (2023 baseline: not applicable) (OP3.1.3)

2a. Designed PUE of 1.4x or lower is achieved (2023 baseline: not applicable)

3a. Number of jobs during construction of data center is at least 21 
(2023 baseline: not applicable) (OP1.2)

4a. One gender equality and diversity policy adopted and implemented h 
(2023 baseline: not applicable) (OP2.3.2) 
Data Source: Data center tiers define levels of resiliency and redundancy for IT facility infrastructure into four tiers. A Tier III data center has 99.982% uptime and less than 1.6 hours downtime annually, while Tier II and I have higher downtime and less resiliency. A &#x201c;Rated 3&#x201d; (Telecommunication Industry Association or TIA 942) data center includes a redundancy assessment for other potential physical risks beyond electrical and mechanical redundancy. Uptime Institute. Tier Classification System. The average annual PUE worldwide is 1.6. Statista. Data Center Average Annual PUE Worldwide from 2007 to 2024. 
Actual value:</narrative>
    </description>
