   <indicator measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1  Indicator 2</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: 1. Access to energy-efficient green data centers in Thailand increased
2. Best practice green data center design and operations demonstrated in a gender-inclusive manner
3. Local employment generated 
4. Gender equality in the workplace enhanced 
Indicator: 2b. At least 3 gender- and disability-inclusive design features integrated in building design that contribute to LEED certification
(2023 baseline: not applicable)

3b. Annual number of jobs provided during operations of data center is at least 32 
(2023 baseline: not applicable) (OP1.2)

4b. One module on gender sensitization and awareness building on the gender equality and diversity policy i included in the onboarding process of staff 
(2023 baseline: not applicable) (OP2.3.2) 
Data Source: The proposed features will contribute to LEED credits as part of Inclusive Design: Pilot Credits by the United States Green Building Council. This may include features such as all-gender and/or family restrooms, the provision of free menstrual hygiene materials, lactation rooms, nondiscrimination policies and procedures, inclusive recruitment, and an inclusive supply chain. 
Actual value:</narrative>
